[2026-05-10T16:59:25.293Z] [STDOUT] Fixes #34

## Summary
- Added a centralized Integram permission utility for legacy `grants`, `role`, and `roleId` state, including READ/WRITE/ADMIN/BARRED normalization.
- Preserved `grants` and `roleId` through API client session restore/save paths, and clear stale legacy permission storage when the active session has no grants.
- Wired migrated table, data table, type editor, dictionary, calendar, info, and directory-admin action visibility/guards to the shared permission checks. Missing permission state now denies write/admin UI actions.
- Added permission fixtures and unit/component coverage for read-only, write, admin, and missing permission contexts.
- Merged `origin/main` into this branch and resolved the table workspace settings/permission conflict.

## Verification
- `npm test` - 37 files, 179 tests passed
- `npm run build` - passed; existing Vite chunk-size warning remains
- `npm run test:e2e` - 35 tests passed

